config APP_WATCHDOG
	bool "Enable task watchdog stall detection"
	default y
	select TASK_WDT
	select WATCHDOG
	select REBOOT
	help
	  Monitors registered tasks with Zephyr's task watchdog and reboots the
	  board if one stops being fed. The failure mode this catches is a hang
	  rather than a CPU fault, which a fatal-error handler cannot see.

	  Coverage is only as good as the channels an application registers: a
	  thread that never registers is not monitored, and a hang inside a
	  workqueue handler is invisible while the registrant keeps feeding.
	  See applications/common/watchdog/app_watchdog.h for the two usage
	  shapes and their trade-offs.

	  With the console coredump backend, a timeout also emits a coredump
	  before rebooting; the flash-partition backend cannot be written from
	  the timeout handler and is skipped.

config APP_REBOOT_ON_FATAL
	bool "Reboot on a fatal error"
	default y
	depends on APP_WATCHDOG
	# Rebooting hides test failures on native_sim.
	depends on !ARCH_POSIX
	select RESET_ON_FATAL_ERROR
	help
	  Reboot as soon as a fatal error has been logged (and any coredump
	  written), instead of halting until the hardware watchdog, if there is
	  one, resets the board CONFIG_TASK_WDT_MIN_TIMEOUT +
	  CONFIG_TASK_WDT_HW_FALLBACK_DELAY later.

	  A fault during boot becomes a reboot loop. An unconfirmed MCUboot
	  image reverts on the next reset, which ends it; a confirmed image
	  keeps looping. Acceptable for a headless device, which would
	  otherwise sit halted until power-cycled.

rsource "../reset_reason/Kconfig"
